# Citation metadata for CTSim (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
#
# Author names and the paper's title/venue/DOI are filled in once the paper is
# final; until then this file exists so GitHub's "Cite this repository" widget
# and Zenodo have something valid to read.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CTSim: a slot-based simulator for consensus over concurrent transmissions"
abstract: >-
  CTSim simulates multi-hop, time-slotted low-power wireless networks and runs
  Paxos, two-phase commit, and total-order multicast over two concurrent-
  transmission physical layers: constructive interference (deterministic,
  pipelined flood rounds) and the capture effect (goal-based rounds with
  in-network merge).
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/sadeqi-ah/ctsim"
authors:
  - name: "The CTSim Authors"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
keywords:
  - distributed consensus
  - concurrent transmissions
  - constructive interference
  - capture effect
  - low-power wireless
  - network simulation
